 {"id":"CF-008","title":"Node lifecycle: supervisor, renew, destroy/rebuild","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":3,"reasoning":"A node's gateway is started with nohup and dies on agent stop/renew; agent TTL is 4h unless renewed. A node that silently disappears is indistinguishable from a node that failed, and cancellation is only possible by killing the process group from a second exec (client kill and --timeout do NOT stop remote work).","acceptance_criteria":"1. The harness runs under a supervisor that restarts it and records restarts. 2. Agent TTL is renewed automatically while the node is active. 3. Cancelling a dispatch kills the process GROUP and the evidence shows it (job pid/pgid written by the job, killed, completion artifact absent after the deadline). 4. destroy then create reproduces the node from recorded commands with no manual step. 5. A node that dies mid-job causes redelivery, and idempotency prevents duplicated work.","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:40:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T18:40:00Z"}
 {"id":"CF-009","title":"P4 — Quick start step 1 (bunker-server-install.sh --check) fails before checking: BUNKER_SERVER is required but documented only later","status":"complete","priority":"P4","complexity":1,"reasoning":"README.md:19 says a stranger starts with: scripts/bunker-server-install.sh --check. Executed verbatim in /home/kara/code-factory, it exits 1 immediately with: scripts/bunker-server-install.sh: line 14: BUNKER_SERVER: set BUNKER_SERVER to your bunker server name. The script reads BUNKER_SERVER before any check; the README documents the export only in the later your-own-infrastructure block (README.md:77-78). A control run with BUNKER_SERVER=invalid reached the checker and returned RESULT: FAIL (2) (server_declared, server_reachable), proving the command works once the variable is set. Fix: in the Quick start, say step 1 requires BUNKER_SERVER (and where the exports live) or move the export block ahead of the quick start commands. ch:trace row=CF-009 spec=specs/NODE.md#layers wave=none:stand-in-tick-no-manifest test=tests/selftest.sh::selftest doc=README.md prompt=prompts/readme.md evidence=docs/audits/code-factory-readme-2026-10-29-21-37-19.md witness=none:local-checkout-and-local-config-only verdict=none:open-finding commit=396f13387a050643898e37f06a6403e02954b07c memory=none:no-durable-record","acceptance_criteria":"1. From a clean env (env -u BUNKER_SERVER) run the exact README command and capture rc=1 plus the exact fatal line. 2. After the README fix, the quick start executed top-to-bottom by a reader with no pre-set env either runs to a RESULT line or documents the required BUNKER_SERVER export before the command that needs it. 3. tests/selftest.sh still prints SELFTEST: PASS.","created_at":"2026-10-29T21:50:15Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T23:25:53Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"f026867f416d7f288810124ff14d0e33a4865300d6eeec96ffa1a54ce2dcf8ca","evidence":[{"run_id":"readme-audit-2026-10-30-20-29-25","ts":"2026-10-30T23:25:53Z","tree_fp":"59f476975